# Agent Core Workflow

You are an expert full-stack engineer in this repository. Write type-safe, performant, self-documenting code.

## Project Overview

**Name:** Lunar Calendar Event Generator
**Goal:** Expand custom lunisolar recurrence rules, monthly 初一/十五 events, and catalog festivals into Gregorian events, then export a downloadable `.ics` file.

### Key Paths

- **Domain Logic:** `src/lib/lunar-dates/` (`cart-expand.ts`, `custom-dates.ts`, `constants.ts`, `lunar-dates.type.ts`)
- **ICS Export:** `src/lib/ics/`
- **State:** `src/store/calendar-store.ts` (Zustand) — one `cart` of `custom`, `monthly`, and `catalog` rows
- **UI:** `src/App.tsx`, `src/components/steps/`, `src/components/cart/` (`CartItemRow`, `CartPickRow`), `src/components/preview/`, `src/components/ui/`; wizard helpers in `src/lib/wizard/`
- **Tests:** `test/`

### Wizard start year (lunar)

The date-selection **start year** is a **lunar year**. `confirmAndExpand` maps the cart to `CartRule[]` and calls `notificationsFromCart` in `cart-expand.ts` with no Jan 1 remap. That helper partitions rows: custom + `kind: 'catalog'` → `collectCustomNotifications`; `kind: 'monthly'` (初一/十五) → `expandMonthlyEvents` (both in `custom-dates.ts`). There is no `conversion.ts`, `milestones.ts`, `getLunarDateNotifications`, or separate `monthlyEvents` store flag. Custom/festival expansion (`expandCustomDate`): leap month only in that start year if it exists; later years use the regular month; day 30 clamps to the last day of the month. Next / Confirm / expand all require a non-empty cart — monthly-only or catalog-only carts are enough.

## Development Environment & Tooling

- **Runtime & Package Manager:** Bun (`bun install`, `bun run`, `bun test`)
- **Frameworks:** TypeScript, React, Tailwind CSS v4, Shadcn UI, Zustand
- **Domain Engines:** `lunar-javascript`, `ts-ics`
- **Lint / Format / Imports:** Biome via Cursor hooks and Lefthook — see `biome.json`; do not add Prettier or ESLint
- **Type Checking:** `bun run typecheck` (`tsc --noEmit`)
- **Testing:** `bun run test` (requires `TZ=Asia/Kuala_Lumpur`). `bunfig.toml` preloads `test/happydom.ts`. Component tests use `@testing-library/react` and `@testing-library/dom`.
- **Git hooks:** Lefthook (`lefthook.yml`). `trustedDependencies` includes `lefthook` and `bun`; `prepare` runs `lefthook install`. Do not add Husky or lint-staged.

## Cursor Hooks

Hooks under `.cursor/hooks/` handle post-edit hygiene. Prefer fixing hook feedback over re-running the same commands after every edit.

| Hook | Responsibility | Not responsible for |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `afterFileEdit` / `afterTabFileEdit` | File-scoped Biome (`check --write`) | `tsc`, tests |
| `postToolUse` (`Write` / `StrReplace` / `EditNotebook`) | Mid-turn `tsc --noEmit` via `additional_context` | Biome, tests |
| `stop` (`loop_limit: 3`) | Final gate: `tsc` + `bun run test` via `followup_message` | Biome / formatting |

`tsc` on both `postToolUse` and `stop` is intentional: early feedback vs don't-finish-red. Only Biome formats; only `stop` runs the test suite.

## Git hooks (Lefthook)

Lefthook is the Git commit/push gate. It does not replace Cursor hooks.

| Hook | Responsibility |
| :--- | :--- |
| `prepare-commit-msg` / `commit-msg` | `[ENG-n]` prefix + commitlint — see `04-commits` |
| `pre-commit` | Biome `check --write` on staged `ts`/`tsx`/`js`/`json`/`html`/`css` (`stage_fixed`) |
| `pre-push` | `bun run typecheck` then `bun run test` |

After clone, `bun install` should install hooks (trusted Lefthook + `prepare`). If Git never runs Lefthook: `bunx lefthook install`. Dry-run: `bunx lefthook run pre-commit` (stage matching files first). Do not use `--no-verify` unless the user asks.

## Common Scripts

- `bun run dev` — hot-reload app (`src/index.ts`)
- `bun run test` — unit tests (stop hook also runs this)
- `bun run typecheck` — TypeScript check (hooks also run this)
- `bun run build` — production build
